#
# The pinned verification costs of prover-smoke (scripts/prover-smoke.sh), in
# heartbeats of the interpreted elaboration (`lake env lean`); a native
# executable counts differently and is not compared with these. A fixture
# named here is elaborated with a stage log, which records the heartbeats of
# each verified target.
#
#   pin   <fixture source> <module::target> <heartbeats>
#   ratio <fixture source> <module::target> <module::target> <quotient>
#
# A target is one record of the log: a target of a module that is verified
# where it is elaborated is `<module>::<target>`, a target of a `verify`
# command has no module in the log and is `::<target>`. No pin is a sum: two
# verified records of one name in a file fail the pin, so a pinned target
# has a name of its own in its file. A pinned target may hold spaces; the
# two targets of a ratio may not.
#
# A measured cost or quotient may differ from its pin by the margin of
# scripts/prover-smoke.sh (COST_MARGIN, 5%) in either direction. Two
# elaborations of one build differed by at most 0.05% on every target below.
# An `initialize` added at one place of the solver's base shifted target
# costs by up to 1.7%; an inert `def` at the top of the same file did not;
# the two interventions differ and the cause is unresolved. The margin is
# what has been observed to leave room for, not a bound: it can alarm falsely.
# Costs complement the fixtures' own expectations and replace none of them.
# A cost under its pin fails too, so that a pin stays where the cost is; that
# is neither a defect nor a reason to re-pin by itself, and a pin says
# nothing of whether the target still proves what it proved: the fixture's
# own expectation does. prover-smoke never writes this file:
# `scripts/prover-smoke.sh --costs` prints every measured figure beside its
# pin, and a pin is changed by hand, with the reason in the commit.
#
# What is pinned: targets of tens of millions of heartbeats; a smaller target
# only with its own measurement beside it. A ratio pairs two sizes of
# the same verification path, not distinct modes: that reduces what moves
# both costs together, it does not cancel it. Two sizes detect a chosen
# regression; they bound no complexity. Each ratio line says what it
# observes.

# The OrderedMap benchmark: the authored generic bodies and the two largest
# scenarios.
pin   ../bench/lean/OrderedMap.lean «0x42».ordered_map::add 88008095
pin   ../bench/lean/OrderedMap.lean «0x42».ordered_map::remove 67906876
pin   ../bench/lean/OrderedMap.lean «0x42».ordered_map::borrow 42320704
pin   ../bench/lean/OrderedMap.lean «0x42».ordered_map::lower_bound_loop 43897059
pin   ../bench/lean/OrderedMap.lean «0x42».ordered_map::lookup_scenario 109881098
pin   ../bench/lean/OrderedMap.lean «0x42».ordered_map::remove_edges_scenario 185951383
# Relative cost, not a size pair: three insertions and a borrow of a present
# key against one insertion and a membership test of an absent key.
ratio ../bench/lean/OrderedMap.lean «0x42».ordered_map::lookup_scenario «0x42».ordered_map::absent_lookup_scenario 2.656
# Relative cost, not a size pair: three insertions, two removals and a borrow
# against three insertions, one removal and a membership test.
ratio ../bench/lean/OrderedMap.lean «0x42».ordered_map::remove_edges_scenario «0x42».ordered_map::remove_scenario 1.264

# A size pair: the same closure target in a module of three sites and in one
# of nine. The cost of the target does not grow with the sites of its module,
# so the quotient stays at one; the targets themselves are small and carry no
# pin of their own.
ratio VerexE2ETests/Check/Closures/KnownSiteCost.lean «0x9b».nine_sites::generic «0x9a».three_sites::generic 1.000

# Quicksort: the authored partition loop over array lemmas, and the recursion.
pin   VerexE2ETests/Check/Examples/Quicksort.lean «0x42».quicksort::partition 139241273
pin   VerexE2ETests/Check/Examples/Quicksort.lean «0x42».quicksort::quick_sort_range 75734391

# A table's invariant at an instance row, and read through a nested table.
# The first is under ten million: it is pinned because its two elaborations
# differed by 0.001% and an unrelated definition at the top of the solver's
# base moved it by 0.03%.
pin   VerexSL/Tests/Shapes/TableRows.lean ::row_instance_ok 9763110
pin   VerexSL/Tests/Shapes/TableRows.lean ::row_nested_ok 20476270

# Two map calls with an optional result, in each representation: the cost of
# the call-contract stages.
pin   VerexSL/Tests/Shapes/Enums.lean ::enum_replaced_ok 22224320
pin   VerexSL/Tests/Shapes/Enums.lean ::vector_replaced_ok 33613040

# Using a function-typed field's behavioural invariants at a call: the
# no-abort rule and the result rule instantiated at the invocation's state.
# Fourteen and a half million, under the tens of millions this file's header
# pins without a measurement of their own: so it is pinned with one, two
# elaborations of one build giving 14505257 and 14502446, 0.019% apart.
pin   VerexSL/Tests/Rendered/mini_amm.lean «0x42».mini_amm::quote 14505257

# A size pair: three and six insertions of distinct keys into a fresh map.
pin   VerexSL/Tests/Cost/MapScaling.lean ::three 43671546
pin   VerexSL/Tests/Cost/MapScaling.lean ::six 85240863
ratio VerexSL/Tests/Cost/MapScaling.lean ::six ::three 1.952
